  <section class="faq" id="faq_click">
    <div class="container">
      <article>
        <!-- <p>Things that you Care about</p> -->
        
                  <h4> FAQs on Student Explore </h4>
        
    </article>
    <article>
      
         
        <section class="faq_acc">
<h3>Q. Is Student Travel Insurance Mandatory?</h3>

<div>
<p>Yes. Many foreign universities ask for Student insurance as a prerequisite for international students.</p>
</div>
</section>

<section class="faq_acc">
<h3>Q. What is the need to buy Student Travel Insurance?</h3>

<div>
<p>Residing in a foreign country for higher studies can be difficult on your pocket, especially if you have an unforeseen emergency ahead of you. Here, student travel insurance comes into play by covering the cost of various medical and non-medical trip contingencies.</p>
</div>
</section>

<section class="faq_acc">
<h3>Q. What do the University Medical Plan Offer?</h3>

<div>
<p>Health insurance offered by foreign universities covers only medical-related coverage with a high premium, co-pay, and sub-limits for treatment.</p>
</div>
</section>

<section class="faq_acc">
<h3>Q. Will my university accept a Student Explore insurance policy?</h3>

<div>
<p>Yes. Student Explore is a comprehensive plan that covers you throughout your higher education in a foreign country. However, reading through the admission documents to understand the requirements before purchasing the policy is always wise.</p>
</div>
</section>

<section class="faq_acc">
<h3>Q. What is the eligible duration for Student Explore?</h3>

<div>
<p>You can get student travel insurance for 1/3/6/9/12/15/18/24 months.</p>
</div>
</section>
 
              </article>
    </div>
  </section>
  
